{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Least Squares.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Least Squares.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear least squares linear least squares","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Least Squares.md","fileName":"Linear Least Squares.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear Least Squares","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 19:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Least Squares Methods]] · [[Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Least Squares Methods","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","Residual Sum of Squares","Normal Equation","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Least Squares.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Least Squares.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear least squares linear least squares","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Least Squares.md","fileName":"Linear Least Squares.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear Least Squares","heading":"Linear Least Squares","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Linear least squares fits a line $y=a+bx$ by minimizing the [[Residual Sum of Squares]]. Setting the derivatives with respect to $a$ and $b$ to zero produces two normal equations.\n\nAlthough the fitted model is a line, the method generalizes directly to several linear parameters by writing the observations as $Ax\\approx b$ and solving the [[Normal Equation]].\n\nThe source applies least squares to outcome vector $Y$ and design matrix $X$, choosing coefficients that minimize the residual sum of squares. This formulation covers group comparisons, continuous predictors, polynomial terms, and interactions within the same matrix framework.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Least Squares Methods","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","Residual Sum of Squares","Normal Equation","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Least Squares.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Least Squares.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear least squares linear least squares","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Least Squares.md","fileName":"Linear Least Squares.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear Least Squares","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Least Squares Methods","Matrix Algebra for Statistical Models","Residual Sum of Squares","Normal Equation","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}